# Paths OpenWiki must not read, in gitignore syntax (psd-dev-standards
# standards/06 section 3). The generated docs pull request merges itself, so
# nothing reviews wiki prose before it lands; this is the hard read boundary
# for internal hostnames, account names, and notes on how credentials are
# handled. It is not a redaction: the wiki can still mention a topic it infers
# from code, tests or commit messages.
#
# Covered here, with what each one carries:
#
#   docs/google-identity-bootstrap.md  Workspace mailbox and group account
#                                      names, OIDC callback URLs, and the
#                                      keyless federation bootstrap steps.
#   docs/phase-2-production-handoffs.md the named Vault subject account and
#                                      the interim personal account it
#                                      replaced, plus outstanding credential
#                                      handoffs.
#   docs/operations/                   restore-drill evidence holding the AWS
#                                      account ID, the SSO role, and the
#                                      operator who ran it.
#   infra/cdk/cdk.context.json         AMI lookup cache keyed by the AWS
#                                      account ID; no design content.
#   infra/terraform/google-identity/identity.auto.tfvars
#                                      Google organization and billing
#                                      account IDs, AWS account IDs.
#   .gitleaksignore                    secret-scanner baseline: where past
#                                      findings sit in the tree.
#
# Secrets themselves never belong in a repo (standards/04 rule 15a); this
# covers the sensitive context that legitimately does.
docs/google-identity-bootstrap.md
docs/phase-2-production-handoffs.md
docs/operations/
infra/cdk/cdk.context.json
infra/terraform/google-identity/identity.auto.tfvars
.gitleaksignore
